# Supabase guidelines

## 1. Clients
- Use `@supabase/ssr` with Next.js App Router.
- Server Components / Actions: `createClient` from `@/lib/supabase/server`.
- Client Components: `createClient` from `@/lib/supabase/client`.
- Service role only on the server (never expose to the browser).

## 2. Security
- Assume RLS on every table in schema `leseno`.
- Check session with `supabase.auth.getUser()` before protected mutations.
- Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`.

## 3. Migrations
- SQL under `supabase/migrations/` with timestamp prefixes.
- Idempotent where practical (`if not exists`, upserts).
